  "Name": "Sflog! CMS 1.0 Arbitrary File Upload Vulnerability",
  "Description": "This module exploits multiple design flaws in Sflog 1.0. By default, the CMS has a default admin credential of \"admin:secret\", which can be abused to access administrative features such as blogs management. Through the management interface, we can upload a backdoor that's accessible by any remote user, and then gain arbitrary code execution.",
